 ['How many days will a 2TB CCTV hard drive record?','There is no reliable answer from capacity alone. Camera count, actual video bitrate, audio, recording hours and usable disk space determine retention. We read the installed settings and compare the estimate with the oldest playable recording.'],
 ['Does adding a larger hard drive improve camera quality?','No. More storage can retain the same streams longer or support a higher recording bitrate, but it does not change the camera sensor, lens or lighting. We agree image-detail requirements before altering stream settings.'],
 ['Can every DVR or NVR accept an 8TB or 16TB drive?','No. Check the exact recorder model, hardware version, supported capacity per drive, number of bays and compatible drive list. A drive that physically fits is not automatically supported.'],
 ['Will I lose recordings when a hard drive is replaced?','New storage does not automatically contain the old recordings. We agree what must be exported before work, verify the exported files on separate storage and label the removed disk. Formatting or initialising can make existing recordings inaccessible.'],
 ['Is motion recording a dependable way to get more recording days?','It can reduce storage use, but savings depend on movement and settings. Missed triggers, delayed starts and incomplete context are possible. Test event recording, pre/post-record buffers and night conditions before relying on it for important evidence.'],
 ['Can H.265 always halve my storage requirement?','No fixed saving is guaranteed. The scene, quality setting, bitrate mode and device implementation matter. Camera and recorder must support the chosen stream, and exported footage must be playable by the customer.'],
